Original commit body from 52e1826ed6d8a3870a23bdd7ddedd26970ea0b5d:

PR #602 removed `TcpListener::bind` and `UdpSocket::bind` as false net_recv
sources. Both rows were ALSO the only function-kind rows their modules carried,
so removing them left each module method-only -- and a repo calling only
`UdpSocket::bind` is now reported method-starved. Three tests asserted the old
shape and broke.

CI ON #602 WAS GREEN, AND THAT IS THE PART WORTH RECORDING. The slicer has no
data-file -> test edge (INV-bigaz), so a YAML-only change selects ~1 test and I
hand-widened the manifest by grepping test filenames for
"io_bound|io_prim|taint|catalog|boundary|verify_claims|nular|vaduk|zumin".
`test_blind_language_method_starvation.py` and `test_associated_fn_kinds.py`
match none of those words. CI ran the manifest, the manifest did not name them,
and a real regression merged green. The full suite -- 24,472 passed, these 2
failed -- is what actually found it. A hand-picked manifest is a hand-picked
blind spot; both files are now IN the manifest.

THE STARVATION REPORT IS CORRECT AND IS KEPT, which is why this repairs the
tests rather than restoring the rows. This file's own bound already decides it:
`test_an_unstamped_call_to_an_UNCATALOGUED_name_still_starves` says a name the
catalogue does not carry in any kind is "exactly what starvation means". After
#602 `UdpSocket::bind` IS such a name.

And the OLD behaviour was a false satisfaction of INV-zubuh's shape: matching
`bind` made the module count as examined while saying nothing whatever about
whether `recv` / `recv_from` had been. One row was vouching for the rest of the
module's surface. The direction is also the safe one -- starvation WITHHOLDS a
verdict rather than granting one, so this trades a false all-clear for an
explicit "not examined". Measured cost on the one rust repo in the INV-nular
A/B cohort (aardvark-dns): no verdict moved.

Pinned as its own named property rather than left as an absence:
test_binding_a_socket_no_longer_vouches_for_its_receive_surface.

Tests: full suite 24,472 passed / 2 failed before this commit; those 2 now pass.
